    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Josh Naylor** (77.77) anchors our lineup as the premier start, benefiting from a high-ceiling matchup against Young. The combination of an elite park factor and a favorable SP xERA of 4.69 creates a prime environment for **Josh Naylor** to deliver power production. Similarly, **James Wood** (68.54) and **Seiya Suzuki** (68.40) represent our most efficient outfield plays. **James Wood** leverages an impressive 0.403 xwOBA and a prime lead-off spot to overcome a tough southpaw matchup, while **Seiya Suzuki** exploits a significant park factor boost to vault into our top-tier tier of starters. **Corbin Carroll** remains a foundational piece of our strategy, as his 88% stolen base efficiency against a slow-delivering pitcher reinforces his necessity in a categories-heavy Roto approach, even against a tougher arm in Gusto.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today involved keeping **Austin Riley** on the bench. Despite a solid 53.41 score, **Austin Riley** was squeezed out by the sheer depth of our middle-infield and corner-infield stability; the optimizer prioritized the higher projected efficiency and specific platoon advantages of players like **Max Muncy** and **Tyler Soderstrom**. While **Tyler Soderstrom** sits at 64.99, his start remains contingent on final lineup confirmation; should he drop in the order or be rested, we have sufficient coverage to adjust. We are keeping a close watch on **Cole Young** (56.14) and **Zach McKinstry** (53.82); both are elevated by favorable park factors, but they carry risks due to their lower batting order positions. As always, the priority for Ghost Ride the WHIP is maintaining our SB edge while avoiding below-floor outings that jeopardize our game caps.",
